      "text": "To determine the range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\), we need to consider the different cases for the expressions \\( |x+1| \\) and \\( |x-1| \\). These expressions change their forms depending on the value of \\( x \\).\n\n### Case Analysis\n\n1. **Case 1: \\( x \\geq 1 \\)**\n   - In this case, both \\( x+1 \\) and \\( x-1 \\) are positive.\n   - Therefore, \\( |x+1| = x+1 \\) and \\( |x-1| = x-1 \\).\n   \\[\n   G(x) = (x+1) - (x-1) = x + 1 - x + 1 = 2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Case 2: \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\)**\n   - Here, \\( x+1 \\) is non-negative and \\( x-1 \\) is negative.\n   - Thus, \\( |x+1| = x+1 \\) and \\( |x-1| = -(x-1) = -x + 1 \\).\n   \\[\n   G(x) = (x+1) - (-x+1) = x + 1 + x - 1 = 2x\n   \\]\n   - Since \\( -1 \\leq x < 1 \\):\n   \\[\n   -2 \\leq 2x < 2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Case 3: \\( x < -1 \\)**\n   - In this case, both \\( x+1 \\) and \\( x-1 \\) are negative.\n   - Therefore, \\( |x+1| = -(x+1) = -x-1 \\) and \\( |x-1| = -(x-1) = -x + 1 \\).\n   \\[\n   G(x) = (-x-1) - (-x + 1) = -x - 1 + x - 1 = -2\n   \\]\n\n### Summary of Function Values for Different Cases\n\n- For \\( x \\in (-\\infty, -1) \\cup [1, \\infty) \\), \\( G(x) = 2 \\).\n- For \\( x \\in [-1, 1) \\), \\( G(x) = 2x \\), which ranges from \\(-2\\) to \\(2\\).\n\nTherefore, combining these results, the overall range of \\( G(x) \\) is all real numbers.\n\n### Final Answer\n\nThe range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(-\\infty, \\infty)}\n\\]",
