      "text": "{eq} \\begin{align} G(x)&= |-x+1|-|x+1|-1\\\\ \\\\ &= |-x+1|-|x+1|-1≥(-1)+(1)-1 \\\\ \\\\ &= -1 \\end{align} {/eq} The function is negative when {eq}-1≤ x≤ 1 {/eq} Thus, the range is {eq}\\boxed{[-1, \\infty )^{-\\!}} {/eq} as shown in the graph.\n\nTo determine the range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function in different intervals of \\( x \\). The critical points where the absolute value expressions change are \\( x = -1 \\) and \\( x = 1 \\). Therefore, we will consider the function in the intervals \\( (-\\infty, -1) \\), \\( [-1, 1] \\), and \\( (1, \\infty) \\).\n\n### Interval 1: \\( x < -1 \\)\n\nFor \\( x < -1 \\), both \\( x+1 \\) and \\( x-1 \\) are negative.\n\\[\nG(x) = -(x+1) - (-(x-1)) = -x-1 - (-x+1) = -x-1 + x-1 = -2\n\\]\n\n### Interval 2: \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\)\n\nFor \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\), \\( x+1 \\) is non-negative and \\( x-1 \\) is non-positive.\n\\[\nG(x) = (x+1) - (-(x-1)) = (x+1) + (x-1) = x+1 + x-1 = 2x\n\\]\n\n### Interval 3: \\( x > 1 \\)\n\nFor \\( x > 1 \\), both \\( x+1 \\) and \\( x-1 \\) are positive.\n\\[\nG(x) = (x+1) - (x-1) = x+1 - x+1 = 2\n\\]\n\n### Summary of the Function in Each Interval\n\n- For \\( x < -1 \\), \\( G(x) = -2 \\).\n- For \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2x \\).\n- For \\( x > 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2 \\).\n\n### Analyzing the Range\n\nTo find the range, we need to determine the minimum and maximum values of \\( G(x) \\).\n\n- The minimum value occurs at \\( x = -1 \\):\n  \\[\n  G(-1) = 2(-1) = -2\n  \\]\n\n- The maximum value occurs at \\( x = 1 \\) (any \\( x \\) in the interval \\([-1, 1]\\) will give a value of \\( G(x) = 2 \\), but the function approaches 2 as \\( x \\) approaches 1 from the left):\n  \\[\n  \\lim_{x \\to 1^-} G(x) = 2(1) = 2\n  \\]\n\nSince \\( G(x) \\) takes on all values between \\(-2\\) and \\(2\\), the range of \\( G(x) \\) is all values from \\(-2\\) to \\(2\\), inclusive.\n\nThus, the range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\) is \\(\\boxed{[-2, 2]}\\).",
